    "vocabulary": [],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What comes to mind when you hear “storybook village”? Do you picture cute little houses with straw roofs? Well, you’re probably thinking of thatched roofs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These lovely rooftops, however, aren’t just found in the worlds of soon-to-be princesses. If you travel around the world, "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "you’ll see them in many different places"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". After all, thatched roofs have been around for thousands of years. They used to be popular everywhere. That’s because the roofing materials were cheap and readily available."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The materials used for thatching vary depending on what grows locally. Reed, a favourite in riverside villages, is one of the strongest materials. It can last between 25 and 40 years. Straw roofs, by comparison, usually last between 15 and 20 years. In Scotland, heather was once a popular material, giving rooftops a reddish colour. It’s less common today, and it takes an experienced thatcher to work with them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A well-built thatched roof doesn’t just look good; it’s also durable. It can, for sure, keep rain from getting into the building. It can also keep pockets of air throughout the roof, allowing the house to stay cool in summer and warm in winter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Sønderho is named Denmark’s most beautiful village. It used to be a busy shipping town. Today, visitors can walk along its peaceful, narrow streets, appreciating the rows of old houses with thatched roofs."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Lying in Japan’s Shogawa River Valley, Ogimachi is known for its unique farmhouses. Their thatched roofs are so "
            },
            {
              "t": "underline",
              "v": "steep"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " that in winter, the heavy snow can slide right off."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The Portuguese"
            },
            {
              "t": "gloss",
              "v": "",
              "zh": "葡萄牙的"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " village of Santana is known for its "
            },
            {
              "t": "em",
              "v": "casinhas de Santana"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "—triangular houses with thatched roofs. The outside is usually painted white, red, and blue, making them look like they belong in a picture book."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "If you travel through the Zambezi Region of Namibia"
            },
            {
              "t": "gloss",
              "v": "",
              "zh": "纳米比亚"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": ", you’ll come across round mud huts with thatched roofs. Thatched roofs can be found across Africa, but the style and roofing materials vary from place to place."
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
